From f1cbd59d69eb14641040705cf57248e55db08021 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:15:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test: write live-test child logs through O_APPEND and read
 them by path (#781)

* test: write live-test child logs through O_APPEND and read them by path

Nineteen gateway/hermes_cli live tests gave a child a 'w+' log handle and
read it with log.seek(0); log.read(). The child inherits that open file
description, so it shares the parent's offset: each seek(0) moved the
child's next write to offset 0, over what was already logged. Most sites
did the seek(0) unconditionally before a readiness assert whose message
reads the log, so on every passing run the offset stayed at 0 and all
later child output overwrote the start of the log; a failure further on
then showed a clobbered log. test_worker_persistence re-seeked on every
worker command. Same race #755 fixed in test_command_discovery.py.

Add tests/child_log.py: ChildLog is an O_APPEND (truncating, like 'w+')
FileIO to pass as the child's stdout/stderr, and text() reads the file by
path. Convert every site whose child can still be writing. Test: a child
writes READY, the shared offset is moved to 0, the child writes NEXT; the
log must read READY\nNEXT\n (without O_APPEND it reads NEXT\n\n).

* test: add unittest-discovery guard to tests/test_child_log.py
